# Lentil Tinga-Style Filling

Adapted from lentils.md research document

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] Optional: 1 [Tbsp olive oil]{ ing="tbsp-olive-oil" } for sauteing
- [ ] 1 large [onion]{ ing="onion" }, diced
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 1 cup [brown lentils]{ ing="brown-lentils" }, rinsed
- [ ] 2 medium [tomatoes]{ ing="tomatoes" }, diced (or 1 can diced tomatoes, 14 oz)
- [ ] 1-2 [chipotle peppers]{ ing="chipotle-peppers" } in adobo, minced
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [adobo sauce]{ ing="adobo-sauce" } (from chipotle can)
- [ ] 1 tsp [dried oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }
- [ ] 2 cups [vegetable broth]{ ing="vegetable-broth" } or water
- [ ] [Salt]{ ing="salt" } to taste

## Recipe

1. (Optional) Saute [onion]{ ing="onion" } and [garlic]{ ing="garlic" } in [olive oil]{ ing="tbsp-olive-oil" } in Instant Pot on saute mode for 2-3 minutes
1. Add [lentils]{ ing="brown-lentils" }, [tomatoes]{ ing="tomatoes" }, [chipotle peppers]{ ing="chipotle-peppers" }, [adobo sauce]{ ing="adobo-sauce" }, [oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }, and [broth]{ ing="vegetable-broth" }
1. Cook on high pressure for 10 minutes
1. Natural release for 10 minutes, then quick release remaining pressure
1. Season with [salt]{ ing="salt" } to taste. If mixture is too liquid, use saute mode to reduce for a few minutes

## Notes

- Versatile filling for tacos, tostadas, burrito bowls, stuffed peppers, or quesadillas
- Adjust chipotle amount based on heat preference (start with 1 pepper for mild)
- Much lower saturated fat than traditional chicken or pork tinga
- Stores well in refrigerator for 4-5 days; freezes well
- Brown lentils (similar to green) hold their shape well for this filling and provide a peppery flavor that complements the smoky chipotle
- For toddlers: Reserve portion before adding chipotle, or serve with cooling toppings like avocado and sour cream
